From 5a857e2ca603fbe973accb86b370d12efac1486a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:54:01 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 wave 18e: allow host-policed drops into web pages

Replace the embedded view delegate's unconditional drop abort with a host drop policy. The host selects which parts of a drag (files, text, URLs, promised image data) reach pages; drags with no accepted part are refused before any page event and mixed drags are filtered at drop. Exact host-registered pasteboard UTIs are rejected in WebContentsViewCocoa itself, so the shell's private sidebar drags never reach web content. Without a policy drops stay aborted, as before. ABI 1.29 / bridge 0.31.0; build p76, native legacy abort, text/URL/file/image drops, private-type invisibility and accept-mask filtering through the real NSDraggingDestination pass.

Last rebased: 2026-11-04 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
